---
import type { MarkdownHeading } from 'astro'
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const registryUrl = new URL('/r/text-bloom.json', Astro.site).href
const installCommand = `npx shadcn@latest add ${registryUrl}`
const createCommand = `npx shadcn@latest init --template vite --name my-app --no-monorepo`
const initCommand = `npx shadcn@latest init`
const usage = `import { TextBloom } from '@/components/ui/kida/text-bloom'

export default function Welcome() {
  return (
    <TextBloom as="h1" voice="pop">
      Make the headline bloom.
    </TextBloom>
  )
}`
const structure = `src/components/ui/kida/
├── text-bloom.tsx
├── text-bloom.css
├── compose-refs.ts
├── use-isomorphic-layout-effect.ts
└── motion/
    ├── text-bloom.ts
    └── reduced-motion.ts`

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'before-you-start', text: 'Before you start' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'prepare-your-project', text: 'Prepare your project' },
  { depth: 3, slug: 'start-a-new-project', text: 'Start a new project' },
  { depth: 3, slug: 'use-an-existing-project', text: 'Use an existing project' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'install-a-component', text: 'Install a component' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'use-the-component', text: 'Use the component' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'understand-the-copied-files', text: 'Understand the copied files' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'copy-manually', text: 'Copy manually' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'troubleshooting', text: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'verify-your-installation', text: 'Verify your installation' },
] satisfies MarkdownHeading[]
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Installation"
  description="Copy a Kida animation into your React project, then customize the source as your own."
  currentPath="/docs/installation"
  headings={headings}
>
  <div class="guide-callout">
    <strong>Copy source, not a package.</strong>
    <p>
      Kida currently uses the shadcn CLI to place readable component files directly in your
      project. There is no unpublished Kida package to install or keep in sync.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>
  <p>You need:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>a React project;</li>
    <li>Node.js and npm, pnpm, yarn, or Bun;</li>
    <li>a shadcn <code>components.json</code> file.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Kida's registry installs public runtime dependencies automatically. You do not need
    <code>@kida-ui/react</code>, <code>@kida-ui/motion</code>, or any other unpublished Kida
    package.
  </p>

  <h2 id="prepare-your-project">Prepare your project</h2>

  <h3 id="start-a-new-project">Start a new project</h3>
  <p>The shadcn CLI can create a configured Vite and React project for you:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={createCommand} lang="bash" />
  <p>
    Choose a component library and preset when prompted, enter the generated directory, then
    continue with the installation command below.
  </p>

  <h3 id="use-an-existing-project">Use an existing project</h3>
  <p>From the root of a shadcn-compatible React project, initialize its configuration once:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={initCommand} lang="bash" />
  <p>
    If the CLI reports missing Tailwind configuration or an import alias, complete the
    <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/installation" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      shadcn framework setup
    </a>
    before continuing.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install-a-component">Install a component</h2>
  <p>Each component page provides its own registry command. For example, install TextBloom:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={installCommand} lang="bash" />
  <p>The command:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>downloads the component from Kida's public registry;</li>
    <li>installs its public runtime dependencies;</li>
    <li>writes the component, styles, and local motion helpers into your project.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you add another Kida component, review any overwrite prompt before accepting it if you
    have already edited a shared helper.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use-the-component">Use the component</h2>
  <p>Import the copied source from your project's configured alias:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={usage} lang="tsx" />
  <p>
    Start your development server and refresh the page to replay viewport-triggered animations.
    Component pages document the available props, variants, accessibility behavior, and live
    examples.
  </p>

  <h2 id="understand-the-copied-files">Understand the copied files</h2>
  <p>A TextBloom installation creates this structure by default:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={structure} lang="text" />
  <p>
    The <code>kida</code> directory namespaces Kida source inside shadcn's conventional
    <code>components/ui</code> directory. Keep the relative structure intact so internal imports
    continue to resolve.
  </p>

  <h2 id="copy-manually">Copy manually</h2>
  <p>
    If you do not want to use the shadcn CLI, open a component page and expand
    <strong>Copy manually</strong>. Install the listed dependencies, create every file at its shown
    target path, and preserve the directory structure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Manual copying is useful when your project does not use shadcn, but the registry command is
    the safer default because it handles dependencies and configured aliases for you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>

  <h3>“A components.json file is required”</h3>
  <p>Run <code>npx shadcn@latest init</code> from your project root, then retry the Kida command.</p>

  <h3>Tailwind or import-alias validation fails</h3>
  <p>
    Finish shadcn's setup for your framework. Confirm that <code>components.json</code> points to
    the same alias your TypeScript and bundler configuration understand.
  </p>

  <h3>The import cannot be resolved</h3>
  <p>
    Check the path created by the CLI. With the default alias, TextBloom is imported from
    <code>@/components/ui/kida/text-bloom</code>. Do not import it from an unpublished
    <code>@kida-ui/*</code> package.
  </p>

  <h3>The component renders but does not animate</h3>
  <p>
    Refresh the page, make sure the element enters the viewport, and check whether your operating
    system requests reduced motion. Kida intentionally avoids non-essential motion when
    <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code> is active.
  </p>

  <h3>The copy button fails</h3>
  <p>
    Allow clipboard access for the site, or select the command directly from the code block and
    copy it with your keyboard.
  </p>

  <h2 id="verify-your-installation">Verify your installation</h2>
  <ol class="verification-list">
    <li>Confirm the expected files exist under <code>src/components/ui/kida</code>.</li>
    <li>Render the component and check the browser console for errors.</li>
    <li>Try its documented variants or options.</li>
    <li>Run your production build, such as <code>pnpm build</code>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A successful production build confirms the copied source, imports, types, and runtime
    dependencies work together outside the Kida repository.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
